    <briefdescription>
<para>A C string operand of a comparator. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The comparators convert the arrays (including the string literals) and the pointers of the character types to this type (see <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1a51e86043001b197561806d5c6297041b" kindref="member">as_operand()</ref></computeroutput>), so that they are compared by content, as a reader of a test expects, and not by address. A null pointer is equal only to another null pointer (not to an empty string), and is less than any string.</para>
<para>The characters are not copied; the operand must outlive the comparison, which is always the case within a check.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Char_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The character type; it satisfies <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1character" kindref="compound">character</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
